WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:13.780
Margaret Thatcher: My friends, we have to
remember these repeated lessons of history.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:20.540
The price of freedom is still, and always
will be, eternal vigilance. Freedom demands

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:26.640
more care and devotion than any other system.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:33.480
Ronald Reagan: It is time that a voice be raised on behalf of the 73 million pointing

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:40.500
out that profit, property rights, and freedom are inseparable, and you cannot have the third

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.900
unless you continue to be entitled to have the first two.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:54.649
Benazir Bhutto: I come here
tonight to address the new realities and find

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:59.160
opportunity in this phase of tragedy.

00:01:04.240 --> 00:01:10.140
Russell Kirk: But American order: freedom, justice, and prosperity,

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:18.560
cannot endure unless America's
public policies are invigorated by imagination.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:25.800
George H.W. Bush: There was a time, not long
ago when Americans were inspired by elected

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:31.320
leaders, and when they trusted them to do
what was best, and when they believed their

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:39.000
leaders shared their hopes and dreams for
the future.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.460
Phil Gramm: What made you who

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:53.299
you are is the freedom and responsibility
you've had. And if we lose it, it's not just

00:01:53.299 --> 00:02:02.899
about prosperity, it's not just about prices,
it's about who we are. It's about our character.

